  "claim": "The FIRE settlement authority boundary is modeled as strict decoding: authority acceptance implies both untrusted settlement delta fields were exact integers, and string-shaped, boolean-shaped, or missing delta fields cannot authorize settlement. The Python runtime and persisted-bundle cross-check are bound to this rule by fail-closed strict type checks and negative regressions.",
